<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/whats-on">What's on</a> shows everything booked at your location for one day or one week. It opens on
        today's <strong>Day</strong> view. For now it shows parties, including the ones imported from Just Step Online.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Moving around">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Day</strong> and <strong>Week</strong> switch between one day and the Monday-to-Sunday week it falls in.</li>
            <li>The arrows go back or forward a day (or a week), and <strong>Today</strong> jumps back to today.</li>
            <li><strong>Go to date</strong> jumps to any date.</li>
            <li>Tick <strong>Show cancelled</strong> to include cancelled parties. They're greyed out and struck through, and never
                counted in the totals.</li>
            <li>Admins get a <strong>Location</strong> picker. Managers see the location they signed in to.</li>
            <li>The address bar keeps the day, view and location, so you can bookmark a view or send the link to another manager.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="The timeline">
        <FluentText>
            On a computer the day is a timeline, with the hours down the left. Each party is a block from its arrival time to its
            finish time, showing the times, the birthday child, how many are coming, the room and the party type. Parties that overlap
            sit side by side, so you can see at a glance when the venue is busiest.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>Dotted lines inside a block mark the <strong>Eat</strong> and <strong>Laser</strong> times, when the party has them.</li>
            <li>A warning icon next to the name means allergies are noted. Hover over it to read them.</li>
            <li>The badge shows whether the party is <strong>Unpaid</strong>, has its <strong>Deposit paid</strong> or is
                <strong>Paid in full</strong>. A dashed edge and a <strong>Provisional</strong> badge mean a hold from Just Step Online
                that isn't confirmed yet.</li>
            <li>On today's timeline a red line marks the time now.</li>
            <li>Click a party to open it, the same as from <a href="/manage/parties">Parties</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            On a phone the day is a list of party cards in time order instead of a timeline, with the same details.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
